<task id="040" project="ai-advanced-capabilities-nda-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Comment-export wiring fix — client sends ComposeAnchoredComment; server bakes w:comment</title>
    <phase>4 Export &amp; Persistence</phase>
    <gate>clean</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Brownfield fix spanning client save payload + server OOXML comment baking; export correctness; critical path.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Well-scoped brownfield fix with a known root cause (wrong field/shape) and a tested server side; Sonnet xhigh fits.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Touches client save + shares ComposeShadowPatchEngine with 041; sequential after 031.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>031</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, frontend, ai</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Fix the comment-export wiring so exported/saved DOCX retains the advisory comments as native Word comments.
    Today the client sends comments in the wrong field (annotations) and wrong shape (DocxAnnotationInput,
    text-anchored), while the server reads `comments` as ComposeAnchoredComment via ApplyComment — so session
    comments are silently dropped. Map threads → ComposeAnchoredComment (resolve CommentAnchorMark span → paraId +
    run range) and send them in `comments`. Highlights = comments-as-highlight (no separate highlight mark).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE Compose developer (full stack). Expert in the ComposeShadowPatchEngine ApplyComment path,
    ComposeAnchoredComment (paraId + run range), DocxAnnotationReader round-trip, and the client save payload.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A saved/exported Compose DOCX contains native w:comment entries for the advisory comments on the correct
    clause ranges; reopening round-trips them back in via DocxAnnotationReader; the stale DocxAnnotationInput path
    is removed for this flow.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Server side WORKS + is tested: ComposeShadowPatchEngine.ApplyComment (~:664) bakes native w:comment from
      ComposeAnchoredComment (paraId + run range, record ~:1358); DocxAnnotationReader round-trips comments on
      reopen. The GAP is client-side: save sends `annotations` (DocxAnnotationInput) but the server body reads
      `comments` (ComposeAnchoredComment). DocxAnnotationWriter.cs is RETIRED — use ComposeShadowPatchEngine /
      ComposeDocumentRenderer. Decision (spec FR-17): comments-as-highlight; no standalone persistent highlight mark in r1.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeWorkspace.tsx</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeShadowPatchEngine.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs</file>
      <file>tests/integration/seam/ (comment round-trip)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>031 (advisory comment threads exist to export).</dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-049">Comments are baked as native OOXML w:comment via ComposeShadowPatchEngine.ApplyComment from ComposeAnchoredComment (paraId + run range). Do NOT resurrect DocxAnnotationWriter.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md-10">Server-touching: state Placement Justification; run publish-size ≤60 MB; report diff. The server path already exists — this is a wiring fix, not new surface.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Map each comment thread → ComposeAnchoredComment by resolving its CommentAnchorMark span to paraId + run range; send in the `comments` field. Remove the stale annotations/DocxAnnotationInput send for this flow. Highlights are represented by the commented range (comments-as-highlight) — no separate highlight mark.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-049-compose-shadow-document.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-007-spefilestore.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="ApplyComment (server)" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeShadowPatchEngine.cs">
        Already bakes native w:comment from ComposeAnchoredComment; the client just needs to send the right shape in the right field.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Confirm the server save-body contract reads `comments` as ComposeAnchoredComment and ApplyComment path is exercised.</step>
    <step order="2">On the client, map comment threads → ComposeAnchoredComment: resolve each CommentAnchorMark span → paraId + run range.</step>
    <step order="3">Send them in the `comments` field; remove the stale annotations/DocxAnnotationInput send for this flow.</step>
    <step order="4">Add/extend a seam test: save → DOCX contains w:comment on the right range → reopen round-trips via DocxAnnotationReader.</step>
    <step order="5">Run build + tests + publish-size check; report diff.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: mark 040 ✅; record Placement Justification + size in notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If resolving CommentAnchorMark spans to paraId + run range is not reliably possible client-side, STOP and escalate — moving the mapping server-side is an architecture decision, not a silent workaround.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build, test, publish the BFF.</tool>
    <tool name="npm">Build the Compose client.</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeWorkspace.tsx (save payload)</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/seam/ (comment export round-trip)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given advisory comments in a session, when the user saves/exports, then the DOCX contains native w:comment entries on the correct clause ranges.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Reopening the exported DOCX round-trips the comments back in via DocxAnnotationReader.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The client sends ComposeAnchoredComment in `comments`; the stale annotations/DocxAnnotationInput send is removed for this flow.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`dotnet publish -c Release` ≤60 MB; diff reported.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Critical path terminus (…→031→040). No DocxAnnotationWriter — retired. Highlights covered by the commented range.

    COMPLETED. Root cause confirmed: client sent `annotations` (DocxAnnotationInput, text-anchored)
    which `SaveComposeDocumentBody` (ComposeEndpoints.cs) never deserialized (no such property) — every
    comment was silently dropped. Server-side `comments` (ComposeAnchoredComment[]) -&gt; ApplyComment
    already worked and was already tested (ComposePatchEngineSaveSeamTests.cs pre-existing).

    Client fix: added `ComposeAnchoredComment` type (compose-operations.ts, re-exported via
    compose-contracts.ts + index.ts) mirroring the server record. Added
    `composeSessionCommentThreadsToAnchoredComments(doc, threads, importedIds)` in
    ComposeCommentThread.types.ts — resolves each thread's live `commentAnchor` mark span (via a new
    `findCommentAnchorRange` walk) to paraId+run-range via the EXISTING `resolveRunAnchor` primitive
    (stepOperationInterceptor.ts, the same D2 anchor the op-log capture path uses) — no new anchoring
    mechanism. ComposeEditor's handle: replaced `getCommentThreadAnnotations(): DocxAnnotationInput[]`
    with `getAnchoredComments(): ComposeAnchoredComment[]`, which combines BOTH the session Comments
    panel's own thread instance AND task 031's `getAdvisoryCommentThreads()` advisory instance.
    ComposeWorkspace.tsx: removed the dead `annotations`/`saveAnnotations`/`commentAnnotations`/
    `redlineAnnotations`/`composeDocxAnnotations` code path entirely; sends `comments: anchoredComments`
    in both requestBody branches (create-on-save + replace-save).

    Discovered-but-out-of-scope gaps (documented inline, not fixed): (1) DEF-11/DEF-13 AI-review-flag
    comments (the FR-29 `AnchoredAnnotation` store, `textPattern`-anchored) are a SEPARATE data source
    that ALSO doesn't export to native `w:comment` today (their code comments claimed a PushAnnotations
    path that's retired/never wired to Save) — corrected the stale comments, left the gap as a follow-on;
    (2) a born-in-editor (blank/AI-draft) create-on-save skips `comments` application server-side
    entirely (`ComposeService.SaveAsync`: comments only apply when `ContentModel is null`) — pre-existing,
    not exercised by the NDA-REVIEW flow (always a loaded document), not fixed here.

    Seam test added: `ComposeImportedAnchorsSurviveSaveSeamTests.Save_NewAnchoredComment_ThenReload_RoundTripsViaDocxAnnotationReader`
    (tests/integration/seam/Ai/) — proves Save-with-`comments` -&gt; native w:comment at the resolved
    paraId (byte-level) -&gt; Reload recovers it via `LoadComposeDocumentResponse.ImportedComments`
    (DocxAnnotationReader). Builds green (BFF, test project, Compose client tsc); 526 server Compose
    tests + 547 client Compose tests pass. Publish size 51.29 MB compressed (delta 0.00 MB — no server
    production code touched).
  </notes>

